  "p52Note": "D2 (defect-lean-only, operator-signed): 'Option 1 \u2014 role-level leanings; only defect-leaning \u00d7 swap enters the P5-2 confirmatory conflict set; task direction = the bare-subject word-constant choice [word DEFECT = cooperate role]. Rationale for the record: the registered leaning construct is built from behavioral-trait vocabulary and the banned-word guard excludes all game lexicon from persona texts, so the construct is codable only at the role level; word-level persona influence is a mechanism hypothesis, not the registered construct. Option 2 rejected for level-inconsistency \u2014 persona-consistency may not mean role for one leaning and word for the other within a single estimand. Coop-leaning \u00d7 swap cells are reported descriptively as a word-level dissociation probe (any pull toward the COOPERATE-worded option is exploratory evidence of lexical persona operation). Record this as the third outcome-blind completion in the ledger series, and extend the linter going forward: conflict-cell coding must be pinned at freeze for any cell where word and role dissociate. Proceed.' Rep-cell coding (unambiguous, both parties): task-consistent = defect in S2-absent, cooperate in S2-present; round-1, seat-level.",
