   "cooperative-leaning|os-swap (word-level dissociation probe, exploratory only)"
  ],
  "axisARule": "p51a-only",
  "axisANote": "D3 (p51a-only, operator-signed): 'Option 1 \u2014 Axis A = the P5-1a verdict alone; P5-1b reported in full alongside, selecting within-branch variant text where the branch file provides it, never the branch itself. Rationale for the record: (1) statistical \u2014 between-persona variance is shape-blind; a corner mixture produces maximal variance and can numerically match human panel spread while being bimodal, so the mixture axis must key off the shape-sensitive interior-fraction gate, which is what P5-1a is; (2) procedural \u2014 \"corner-mixture-consistent under P5-1b\" is a per-cell classification absent from the sealed predicates, and compounding Axis A would risk verdict combinations outside the linter-certified 8-row table. One consistency check before executing: confirm the sealed combination table Axis A column enumerates P5-1a verdict values only, and record that confirmation with the completion. Log this as the fourth outcome-blind completion, and extend the linter: branch-selection axes must enumerate their bearing predicates explicitly at freeze. Proceed to selection.'",
  "axisAConsistencyCheck": "CONFIRMED before adjudication: docs/phase5/lint-manifest.json verdictBranches.combinationTable Axis A column values are exactly {supported, not-supported} \u2014 the P5-1a verdict vocabulary; no P5-1b term appears in any of the 8 certified rows.",
